---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About MathsIsCool — Free Math Reference for Students" description="Learn about MathsIsCool — the free, colorful math reference site with multiplication tables, formulas and more for students worldwide." currentPage="about">
<div class="page">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <h1>About <span style="color:var(--owl-brown)">MathsIsCool</span> 🦉</h1>
    <p>Your friendly neighborhood math professor — free, colorful, and for everyone!</p>
  </div>
  <div class="seo-content">
    <h2>Who is Professor Hoot?</h2>
    <p>Professor Hoot is MathsIsCool's mascot — a wise, friendly owl dressed as a math teacher, complete with round glasses, a bow tie, and a math textbook. He appears throughout the site to make learning feel fun and approachable, whether you're 8 years old learning times tables or 18 studying integration formulas.</p>
    <h3>Why We Built MathsIsCool</h3>
    <p>Most math reference websites are either ugly, boring, or stop at Grade 5. Students preparing for CBSE boards, GCSE exams, competitive entrance tests, or university calculus had to jump between multiple ugly sites to find what they needed. MathsIsCool brings everything together in one colorful, well-organized, mobile-friendly site — completely free.</p>
    <h3>What We Cover</h3>
    <p>Multiplication tables from 1 to 50 (most sites stop at 12!), squares and cubes up to 50, square roots and cube roots, all algebra identities, complete differentiation and integration formula lists, trigonometry tables, Roman numerals, and prime numbers — with more content added regularly.</p>
    <h3>For Every Student</h3>
    <p>MathsIsCool is designed for global students — CBSE, ICSE, GCSE, A-Level, IB, Common Core, and competitive exam students will all find what they need here. Our colorful design makes it welcoming for young learners while the content depth serves older students and parents helping with homework.</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
